{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it","id":1455312,"title":"Baali or infernalists as Player Characters - doable or not and how do you do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-21T10:15:09-07:00","id":1455312,"title":"Baali or infernalists as Player Characters - doable or not and how do you do it?","content":"Greetings, <br /> <br /> Is it doable to have a Baali (or an infernalist) player character in a group when everybody is on board?<br /> We have at our disposal clanbook - baali (black dog), all the V20 books and from storyteller vault the 2 books related to baali.<br /> We also have path of screams, book of madness and devil's due from old lines to look into. (have been playing for well over 2 decades)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are there any tips and tricks to make this work? (except of course the part about don't go into details which should remain unnamed and we have easy stops if it should not work out,...) I'm asking cause this is the first time we are going to play the &quot;bad guys&quot;, if there is something like good guys in the world of darkness....</li> <li>Is there any way to make demonic investments works because as they have no XP component, they scale pretty harshly?</li> <li>Are there any other books we might need?</li> </ol>Thank you very much for any and all advice even if it's, don't do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T12:45:41-07:00","id":1455322,"title":"","content":"1: Just hope that he's a good player with experience playing 'normal' vampires. &quot;Chaotic evil&quot; is not a license to be stupid. Try your best to be impartial; Don't stack things against him because his character is morally reprehensible, stack things against him when he's left evidence around that he's a threat to the status quo. Vampire's are too politically inclined to do the right thing; Not everyone's going to try to purge the witch for dealing with a devil, blackmail is a likely option.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2: Look at werewolf. most Investments are essentially Gifts. Optionally, you can make them cheaper by pairing flaws with the gifts. Moderating what 'gifts' the player can take/what level they are is important, because just granting the vampire werewolf gifts at the level werewolves get them can be a terrible mistake. But 3/4/5x level is fairly balanced; take your pick. Alternatively, every downtime you could let your players allocate time to gathering backgrounds/rituals, and allow the infernalist to use this time to secure new deals (which distracts them from gaining backgrounds) <br /> <br /> 3. Freak legion's cool. Not the same thing, but relevant enough. KotE had an interesting system for infernalism, but I haven't touched those books for a wihle. <br /> Use DAV20 for Diamonion. It's not perfect, but it's by far the best version. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T16:34:24-07:00","id":1455334,"title":"","content":"I've never tried to make demonic investments work for anyone who isn't an NPC. <br /> <br /> If you have the Demon: the Fallen core rulebook and/or Damned and Deceived, the supplement for Demon players' thralls, I'd recommend using the system for thralls as a substitute for investments. For every point of Faith that a human thrall's pact would cost them, substitute one extra point of Blood lost every day instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T19:50:26-07:00","id":1455339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455322#post1455322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: Just hope that he's a good player with experience playing 'normal' vampires. &quot;Chaotic evil&quot; is not a license to be stupid. Try your best to be impartial; Don't stack things against him because his character is morally reprehensible, stack things against him when he's left evidence around that he's a threat to the status quo. Vampire's are too politically inclined to do the right thing; Not everyone's going to try to purge the witch for dealing with a devil, blackmail is a likely option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you that nobody plays chaotic stupid since we have been playing together for a while now. The Goal is to be impartial towards the infernalist but also not to give him free reign but good remark about vampires being mostly political motivated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455322#post1455322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Look at werewolf. most Investments are essentially Gifts. Optionally, you can make them cheaper by pairing flaws with the gifts. Moderating what 'gifts' the player can take/what level they are is important, because just granting the vampire werewolf gifts at the level werewolves get them can be a terrible mistake. But 3/4/5x level is fairly balanced; take your pick. Alternatively, every downtime you could let your players allocate time to gathering backgrounds/rituals, and allow the infernalist to use this time to secure new deals (which distracts them from gaining backgrounds)</div> </div> </div> </div>For investments we had looked at the books that we mentioned above. An idea we have been toying with is to ask for a level 6 daimoinon investment. You can mostly place anything under there since it gives a ST licence to approve. Gifts had not figured into the equation at this point in time but that is possible. For backgrounds we also use an xp cost since otherwise there is a randomness we kinda don't like so that would make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455322#post1455322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Freak legion's cool. Not the same thing, but relevant enough. KotE had an interesting system for infernalism, but I haven't touched those books for a wihle.<br /> Use DAV20 for Diamonion. It's not perfect, but it's by far the best version.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Daimoinon (or is it Daimonion?) we are going to use DAV20, so that wors out perfectly. We'll check freak legion also, same as the KotE books though KotE might be the one line we are missing between players and ST. We'll see what we can dig up, thanks for the tip.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T19:53:48-07:00","id":1455340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455334#post1455334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never tried to make demonic investments work for anyone who isn't an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither have we an that is kinda the reason for this post, since we want to see if anybody else found some things to be aware of. Somehow I am kinda glad not everybody is just playing infernalists left and right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455334#post1455334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the Demon: the Fallen core rulebook and/or Damned and Deceived, the supplement for Demon players' thralls, I'd recommend using the system for thralls as a substitute for investments. For every point of Faith that a human thrall's pact would cost them, substitute one extra point of Blood lost every day instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest we had not looked into demon: the fallen in that fashion though we do have the line available for perusal. The fact that vampires can't make pacts with &quot;DTF demons&quot; kinda blew that out of the option list for us. Your idea of it costing an extra bloodpoint every day upon awakening per faith would demand a recurring cost which could/would offset free powers. I need to mull over that idea if it would actually work out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T20:11:39-07:00","id":1455342,"title":"","content":"I guess my question is, is the player going for one of the absolutely, irredeemably evil puppet-of-the-demon-lord Baali, or is he going for one of the Order of Molochim which, while still evil, at least commits those evil with the greater good of the world in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T23:07:11-07:00","id":1455346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455342#post1455342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my question is, is the player going for one of the absolutely, irredeemably evil puppet-of-the-demon-lord Baali, or is he going for one of the Order of Molochim which, while still evil, at least commits those evil with the greater good of the world in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked the Player how he sees it and it's kinda of a middle ground. He doesn't want to be an evil puppet of the demon lord Baali but neither does he want to be one of those trying to put the children of the outer dark to sleep.<br /> <br /> How I understood it, he wants to take the power of darkness and harness it for his own purposes and if something would awaken the children, he'll help prevent that because that would compromise his source of power but he won't constantly be working towards that goal. He is also all for the principle of bartering other people their souls to get &quot;rewards&quot; and &quot;corrupt&quot; them to serve his purposes and goals. Though the latter regarding corruption more from a cult, provide me more souls, chaff, resources point of view. <br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T03:49:17-07:00","id":1455359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455346#post1455346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked the Player how he sees it and it's kinda of a middle ground. He doesn't want to be an evil puppet of the demon lord Baali but neither does he want to be one of those trying to put the children of the outer dark to sleep.<br /> <br /> How I understood it, he wants to take the power of darkness and harness it for his own purposes and if something would awaken the children, he'll help prevent that because that would compromise his source of power but he won't constantly be working towards that goal. He is also all for the principle of bartering other people their souls to get &amp;quot;rewards&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;corrupt&amp;quot; them to serve his purposes and goals. Though the latter regarding corruption more from a cult, provide me more souls, chaff, resources point of view. <br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like a Nergali to me, albeit a slightly more pragmatic one. That's more Chaotic Evil territory, but it could be Neutral Evil with the right balance.<br /> <br /> KotE has a good system for investments, as others have said, and probably meshes the best with V20 since it uses Revised rules.<br /> <br /> I would consider whether he's 'out' as a Baali or whether he poses as Tremere (a common con, since the Tremere and Baali share a blood link via Saulot). The latter would make more sense, since Baali are uniformly hunted.<br /> <br /> You could perhaps have him pretend to be Malkavian (superficially, some Daimonion powers look like Dementation at the lower levels), but I think Tremere is an easier cover to maintain unless there are loads of Tremere in your setting who will notice he isn't part of the Pyramid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T04:50:54-07:00","id":1455363,"title":"","content":"I am probably unique in the fact that I don't see a reason why Infernalist Sabbat are any worse than regular Sabbat. Then again, my favorite game was Demon: The Fallen so I take the view that demons are not particularly worse than most supernaturals or humanity.<br /> <br /> Which is awful.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T06:47:27-07:00","id":1455367,"title":"","content":"I mean I can agree with that. The Sabbat are pretty damn monstrous, and I imagine the Tzimisci can get up to stuff that even Demons go, &quot;Whoa, whoa, whoa, stop. That's not cool.&quot; That said, the Sabbat consider Infernalists to be the absolute worst because they sacrifice their much vaunted freedom for slavery, and their loyalty to the Sabbat inevitably becomes secondary (if that) to their loyalty to their demon lord. So they see a huge distinction between themselves and Infernalists, but from most outsiders perespectives they probably don't see much of a difference in the general day-to-day activities of a Sabbat or Infernalist Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T07:08:25-07:00","id":1455370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455359#post1455359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KotE has a good system for investments, as others have said, and probably meshes the best with V20 since it uses Revised rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you refer to those in the book <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/453/The-1000-Hells\" target=\"_blank\">1000 Hells</a> page 111-113 where there are some sample investments? I looked at those but don't really get why you consider them as a good system since they follow the same reasoning as other books? Or is there something very obvious I missed? Or are you referring to another book altogether?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455359#post1455359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would consider whether he's 'out' as a Baali or whether he poses as Tremere (a common con, since the Tremere and Baali share a blood link via Saulot). The latter would make more sense, since Baali are uniformly hunted.You could perhaps have him pretend to be Malkavian (superficially, some Daimonion powers look like Dementation at the lower levels), but I think Tremere is an easier cover to maintain unless there are loads of Tremere in your setting who will notice he isn't part of the Pyramid.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are at this point in time still far in the BCE era, so posing as another clan is an option but probably not a Tremere since they aren't around yet for quite some time. The player is however asking if he could be part of the creation of Clan Tremere or the cursing of Clan Assamite, that seems to have a lot of appeal to him. The creation of Clan Tremere is apparently something he read in a novel, that Baali would be involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T07:13:13-07:00","id":1455371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455363#post1455363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am probably unique in the fact that I don't see a reason why Infernalist Sabbat are any worse than regular Sabbat. Then again, my favorite game was Demon: The Fallen so I take the view that demons are not particularly worse than most supernaturals or humanity.<br /> <br /> Which is awful.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can relate to parts of this. The reason we have not played anything like this before is that people tend to &quot;overcompensate&quot; to prove how &quot;infernalist&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; they can be. We have however in other gamelines had evil games where the players were evil, but not stupid evil. Just very selfishly evil and at time destructive and domineering evil but never evil for evil's sake. That is what we are trying to stay away from, since that would change the game into something nobody wants to play. At least, that is how I view it.<br /> <br /> I think personally that infernalist sabbat are lacking the &quot;higher purpose&quot; that regular sabbat members have. Never mind the elders but the call of: freedom of choice, no oppression. Basically, the whole propaganda the sabbat is about. In the case of the Infernalist that illusion ceases to exist, you are at any moment in time just one mistake away from being a slave instead of a lord. For a Baali, whose clan name comes from the word Ba'al or lord, that would be the worst possible outcome. At least that is how I view it, feel free to disagree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T07:15:55-07:00","id":1455372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455367#post1455367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I can agree with that. The Sabbat are pretty damn monstrous, and I imagine the Tzimisci can get up to stuff that even Demons go, &quot;Whoa, whoa, whoa, stop. That's not cool.&quot; That said, the Sabbat consider Infernalists to be the absolute worst because they sacrifice their much vaunted freedom for slavery, and their loyalty to the Sabbat inevitably becomes secondary (if that) to their loyalty to their demon lord. So they see a huge distinction between themselves and Infernalists, but from most outsiders perespectives they probably don't see much of a difference in the general day-to-day activities of a Sabbat or Infernalist Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fully agree with this. If you are on the receiving end of the ministrations of a Tzismisce on the path of Metamorphosis or the ministrations of an infernalist on the path of evil revalations, you are f***ed either way and your (un)life is hopefully going to be very short... For an outsider, both are monsters of the first order to put it gently...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T08:25:22-07:00","id":1455382,"title":"","content":"That the Sabbat makes anti-infernalism such a priority lends itself to a reading in which it was starting to become an embarrassingly common problem before they started cracking down. Anything for an edge against the enemy and all that.<br /> <br /> It also lends itself to a reading in which Galbraith simply wanted to throw suspicion off of herself, and a third in which she simply didn't want any competition for her master's favor. <br /> <br /> (I prefer the third one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T08:40:45-07:00","id":1455384,"title":"","content":"Imo it's a group effort, the rest of the players have to be cool with it, the player themselves can't be an edge lord and the st has to be mature enough to balance everything out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T09:36:21-07:00","id":1455387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455382#post1455382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Sabbat makes anti-infernalism such a priority lends itself to a reading in which it was starting to become an embarrassingly common problem before they started cracking down. Anything for an edge against the enemy and all that.<br /> <br /> It also lends itself to a reading in which Galbraith simply wanted to throw suspicion off of herself, and a third in which she simply didn't want any competition for her master's favor.<br /> <br /> (I prefer the third one.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I utterly forgot about Galbraith being an infernalist. We saw that in Chaos Factor but I understood the book was retconned after that or dismissed? Or did I misunderstand that?<br /> But yes, everything which gives you an edge is fair game but infernalism is changing one set of manacles, for another from the Sabbat their point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T09:37:15-07:00","id":1455388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455384#post1455384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo it's a group effort, the rest of the players have to be cool with it, the player themselves can't be an edge lord and the st has to be mature enough to balance everything out</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very true. We're all in this together. Everybody is on board and the players are none of them edge lords so that should work out. And I sincerely hope the ST is mature enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T13:16:06-07:00","id":1455395,"title":"","content":"I assume it remained canon, not least because it provides a motive for Elimelech to have taken her out; but that can always be the subject of another thread instead of derailing this one any further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T03:20:11-07:00","id":1455428,"title":"","content":"The scary thing about Infernalism, as far as vampires go, isn't the demon from hell that's an embodiment of evil, it's the disruption of social order and the threat to the established hierarchy. <br /> Infernalism allows neonates a quick boost in power that can have them rival elders; The established powers have spend centuries getting to where they are now, they aren't going to want neonates looking at them like equals and demanding concessions. Especially in the Sabbat, where the emphasis on personal strength and the legality of duels make infernalism an enticing cheat, plus there's many neonates, relatively good amounts of elders, but very few Ancillae (presumably because they're a massive internal threat to most elders and so they are moved towards more dangerous missions with high attrition rates) <br /> <br /> Split loyalties is really secondary, though still very important. There are infernalists that actually dominate demons rather than the other way round, but they're lumped in with the ones who are loyal to demons. Why? Because it's primarily a concern of power, not &quot;loyalty&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T10:46:10-07:00","id":1455448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455395#post1455395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it remained canon, not least because it provides a motive for Elimelech to have taken her out; but that can always be the subject of another thread instead of derailing this one any further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it cannon that he did? All I read is that they didn't know who did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T10:48:27-07:00","id":1455449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455428#post1455428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scary thing about Infernalism, as far as vampires go, isn't the demon from hell that's an embodiment of evil, it's the disruption of social order and the threat to the established hierarchy.<br /> Infernalism allows neonates a quick boost in power that can have them rival elders; The established powers have spend centuries getting to where they are now, they aren't going to want neonates looking at them like equals and demanding concessions. Especially in the Sabbat, where the emphasis on personal strength and the legality of duels make infernalism an enticing cheat, plus there's many neonates, relatively good amounts of elders, but very few Ancillae (presumably because they're a massive internal threat to most elders and so they are moved towards more dangerous missions with high attrition rates)<br /> <br /> Split loyalties is really secondary, though still very important. There are infernalists that actually dominate demons rather than the other way round, but they're lumped in with the ones who are loyal to demons. Why? Because it's primarily a concern of power, not &quot;loyalty&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually never looked at it this way but yes, with the boost &quot;cheat&quot; that demons give, even a &quot;neonate&quot; could become a monster. I think that characters like Dylan Bruce are an example of this which is well worked out. Infernalism really rocks the boat in many ways and breaks a lot of &quot;certitudes&quot; regarding the way things should go.<br /> <br /> So that is really an interesting angle. It's a surprise that so many manage to survive though, but that might be due to the scale and the limited resources to fish them out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T11:01:49-07:00","id":1455452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455370#post1455370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you refer to those in the book <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/453/The-1000-Hells&amp;quot;]1000</a> Hells[/URL] page 111-113 where there are some sample investments? I looked at those but don't really get why you consider them as a good system since they follow the same reasoning as other books? Or is there something very obvious I missed? Or are you referring to another book altogether?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We are at this point in time still far in the BCE era, so posing as another clan is an option but probably not a Tremere since they aren't around yet for quite some time. The player is however asking if he could be part of the creation of Clan Tremere or the cursing of Clan Assamite, that seems to have a lot of appeal to him. The creation of Clan Tremere is apparently something he read in a novel, that Baali would be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be remembering them being longer than they were... So maybe try Book of Madness Revised instead? It's been a long time since I've looked at Infernalism.<br /> <br /> If it's BCE, Salubri make a good option. But as Baali allegedly are cousins of the Old Can Tzimisce, you could go with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T14:50:00-07:00","id":1455466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455448#post1455448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is it cannon that he did? All I read is that they didn't know who did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vasantasena names him as the killer in BJD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T18:36:30-07:00","id":1455591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455428#post1455428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scary thing about Infernalism, as far as vampires go, isn't the demon from hell that's an embodiment of evil, it's the disruption of social order and the threat to the established hierarchy.<br /> Infernalism allows neonates a quick boost in power that can have them rival elders; The established powers have spend centuries getting to where they are now, they aren't going to want neonates looking at them like equals and demanding concessions. Especially in the Sabbat, where the emphasis on personal strength and the legality of duels make infernalism an enticing cheat, plus there's many neonates, relatively good amounts of elders, but very few Ancillae (presumably because they're a massive internal threat to most elders and so they are moved towards more dangerous missions with high attrition rates)<br /> <br /> Split loyalties is really secondary, though still very important. There are infernalists that actually dominate demons rather than the other way round, but they're lumped in with the ones who are loyal to demons. Why? Because it's primarily a concern of power, not &quot;loyalty&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's rare but I totally agree this is the real reason the Sabbat doesn't want infernalists to thrive and vice versa in other sects.<br /> <br /> Infernalists can become as powerful as Elders, depending on what sort of deals they make and how well they follow through on it. Demons are unpredictable because they may want to just screw with their summoners or they might be happy to form a long-lasting profitable relationship with the worshiper.<br /> <br /> It's the choice between summoning a Luciferian or Ravener.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T18:10:15-07:00","id":1455634,"title":"","content":"Played a Baali in a game before, had a blast and so did the ST. One of my favorite PC's to this day. He was this disenfranchised former crusader, who was burned alive and badly disfigured before the Embrace, who was on the Path of the Devil and actually a Furore. Mind that path actually looks upon infernalism with fairly great disdain (because ultimately, the infernalist is leashing themselves to demons), and being he was essentially a proto-Anarch he actually wasn't a &quot;bad&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> It's just that his methods in fighting the tyranny of the elders, by taking the fight to them, were...not what one would call tasteful.<br /> <br /> It's about the same as a Typhonist, RoK Ventrue, high Humanity or Road of Heaven anything, Salubri, Brujah rolled with low Self-Control, Malkavian, RoK (or Abyss) Lasombra, literally any Ravnos ever made, that poor fuck who rolls a Cappadocian in a Dark Ages game thinking they're gonna be the one to beat the odds, wareadors (who admittedly are fun as fuck), or <i>that guy</i> who rolls <i>hard</i> into the &quot;survivalist loner&quot; Gangrel stereotype. It's not what you're playing, it's how you're playing it.<br /> <br /> Baali are, on their own, no more or less potentially disruptive than anything I listed above and more. The bottom line is, make a character with a compelling backstory whose schemes and behavior doesn't outright fuck with other PC's or the chronicle in sum; if that character happens to be a Baali and fits, <i>great</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:35:41-07:00","id":1455665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455452#post1455452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be remembering them being longer than they were... So maybe try Book of Madness Revised instead? It's been a long time since I've looked at Infernalism.<br /> <br /> If it's BCE, Salubri make a good option. But as Baali allegedly are cousins of the Old Can Tzimisce, you could go with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware Baali are cousings of the Old Clan Tzimisce?<br /> But thank you for the advise.<br /> <br /> Choosing the Salubri would indeed be &quot;ironic&quot; but wouldn't that force me to learn obeah/valeren to masquerade as a salubri or would it be possible to fake one without the &quot;third eye&quot;?<br /> Any tips regarding this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:36:49-07:00","id":1455667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455466#post1455466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vasantasena names him as the killer in BJD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I utterly missed that... Thank you, I kinda feel like I learned something really cool today! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:39:30-07:00","id":1455669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455591#post1455591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's rare but I totally agree this is the real reason the Sabbat doesn't want infernalists to thrive and vice versa in other sects.<br /> <br /> Infernalists can become as powerful as Elders, depending on what sort of deals they make and how well they follow through on it. Demons are unpredictable because they may want to just screw with their summoners or they might be happy to form a long-lasting profitable relationship with the worshiper.<br /> <br /> It's the choice between summoning a Luciferian or Ravener.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the moment the Baali is not making demonic pacts (yet) so no clue what he is going to find or encounter or how it is going to be. Not every demon is made equal as you yourself kinda point out. So it might depend on what the story needs or how things progress I guess.<br /> <br /> I still have the feeling somehow that infernalist PC's kinda become scary very quickly due to how &quot;investments&quot; stack, even with some of them having drawbacks. I mean, it might be that I'm reading something wrong but as long as you roleplay your but off, keep it stupid simple and don't get overconfident, they can take you a very long way. Then again, that is the recipe for success for any player in any rpg so ... the point might be moot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:43:11-07:00","id":1455671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455634#post1455634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Played a Baali in a game before, had a blast and so did the ST. One of my favorite PC's to this day. He was this disenfranchised former crusader, who was burned alive and badly disfigured before the Embrace, who was on the Path of the Devil and actually a Furore. Mind that path actually looks upon infernalism with fairly great disdain (because ultimately, the infernalist is leashing themselves to demons), and being he was essentially a proto-Anarch he actually wasn't a &quot;bad&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> It's just that his methods in fighting the tyranny of the elders, by taking the fight to them, were...not what one would call tasteful.<br /> <br /> It's about the same as a Typhonist, RoK Ventrue, high Humanity or Road of Heaven anything, Salubri, Brujah rolled with low Self-Control, Malkavian, RoK (or Abyss) Lasombra, literally any Ravnos ever made, that poor fuck who rolls a Cappadocian in a Dark Ages game thinking they're gonna be the one to beat the odds, wareadors (who admittedly are fun as fuck), or <i>that guy</i> who rolls <i>hard</i> into the &quot;survivalist loner&quot; Gangrel stereotype. It's not what you're playing, it's how you're playing it.<br /> <br /> Baali are, on their own, no more or less potentially disruptive than anything I listed above and more. The bottom line is, make a character with a compelling backstory whose schemes and behavior doesn't outright fuck with other PC's or the chronicle in sum; if that character happens to be a Baali and fits, <i>great</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm really glad somebody else played a baali and I think you nailed it. Any character concept can become disruptive to a chronicle/story and any character if played correctly can fit in. Even crossover campaigns of which we have played quite a few (remember very fondly a campaign in ancient china) are workable if everybody stays sane and allows each other the time to shine and the time to play their character. basically, the way RP is meant to be. The characters are the medium, the tools and the players are the drivers, heart and soul. And the medium is not the limitation, the players most often are. <br /> <br /> Could you share some of the (cool) things you did and why and how you did them? Always interested in stories regarding this and I imagine quite a few other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:53:11-07:00","id":1455673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455665#post1455665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't aware Baali are cousings of the Old Clan Tzimisce?<br /> But thank you for the advise.<br /> <br /> Choosing the Salubri would indeed be &quot;ironic&quot; but wouldn't that force me to learn obeah/valeren to masquerade as a salubri or would it be possible to fake one without the &quot;third eye&quot;?<br /> Any tips regarding this?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC this is more a theory than a fact. I think the V20 Black Hand book introduced the idea that the Eldest may have created the original three Baali (the &quot;original three&quot; &quot;commonly&quot; known, anyways). The Molochim are also presented as having a close working relationship with the Old Clan in there, but that's more affiliation than blood relation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T13:33:57-07:00","id":1455679,"title":"","content":"Back as far as Revised I recall some books mentioning Baali flooding into Eastern Europe in response to Kupala's increased activity, and contact with the Old Clan that resulted in sharing of ideas and philosophies. I think there's enough common ground in mysticism and bending spirits to one's will that an actual blood tie between the two groups isn't needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T18:47:19-07:00","id":1455690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455671#post1455671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you share some of the (cool) things you did and why and how you did them? Always interested in stories regarding this and I imagine quite a few other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character concept was very specific and therefore likely to not be applicable or relevant to all, or most, campaigns. The ST knew I'd have a hard row to hoe, so allowed me a key merit to the concept: Unholy Aura. It's basically anti-True Faith, and has more or less inverse, ongoing, role play and mechanical prerequisites. So, considering that merit, the character was basically an Inquisitor hunter.<br /> <br /> Remember, disenfranchised crusader. That character <b><i>hated</i></b> the Church, and all would-be tyrants and manipulators. Lasombra in particular held the character's ire, being as they are a crossover of both worlds.<br /> <br /> That was a short-lived TC game that made it to the Dracula stuff before it disbanded, due to time constraints for the ST, and general dislike of the Dracula stories without a clear idea how to cut the content and still make it work. In the 1413 story there's a particularly nasty fight with an Inquisitor, that ended up being a complete non-starter when that Inquisitor's faith backlashed against him when used against my character. The Inquisitor's faith broke, and my character embraced him on the spot; the character wasn't about to let him live, so he staked the Inquisitor with his eyes open, crucified him against the east-facing wall of the church, covered him in pitch, and stacked a good amount of wood beneath and around him, also covered in pitch.<br /> <br /> So, my character just <i>shattered</i> the Inquisitor's faith. Then, he embraced the inquisitor, forever damning his soul. Then, when the sun rose and the Inquisitor caught fire, he'd meet final death in Rotschreck-aggravated agony, and the fire would catch, spread, and burn down the church.<br /> <br /> That story, the PC's are basically screwed no matter what. Nova Arpad's involved, and the best they can hope for is not to piss her off, and that's if they managed to achieve every last goal set before them and with flying colors (an almost impossible task). My character...well, not only did he actively sabotage Nova's plans, he quite obviously and deliberately broke the Silence of the Blood several times over in her own backyard, then proceeded to straight fucking murder an Inquisitor and burn down a church, practically guaranteeing job security for my character for the foreseen future.<br /> <br /> So, needless to say the seventh-generation Ventrue elder was <b><i>pissed</i></b>. To which my character told her, to her face, to fuck off because she had neither the clout nor leverage to make good on her threats, she was well out of time and goodwill with the Tremere and Ventrue, and she'd be lucky to survive the decade with no allies and no favors amidst an Anarch revolt. I'd been using Daimonion on her ever since the first story, so my character and a nice, neat little arsenal of self-doubt, uncertainty, mental trauma, and fear to nail her with Fear the Void and Psychomachia. Torpored her on the spot.<br /> <br /> Her staked body made a nice little decoration for my character's new domain, at least until my character ransomed it off for formal recognition of my character's praxis from the Tremere and the establishment of a chantry in his domain. Filled of course, with Tremere that were totally Tremere and not at all Baali infiltrators, because Baali blood is for some reason indistinguishable from Tremere blood to all but the most practiced blood sorcerers.<br /> <br /> The ST was laughing his ass off, because he knew I was biding my time and chomping at the bit to pull <i>something</i>, but he didn't expect me to go from zero to nuclear at the drop of a hat and with zero hesitation. The other players...they'd all been my friends for years at the time, and we'd gamed plenty together in non-VtM games, but they were <i>horrified</i> out of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-27-2021, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T00:36:03-07:00","id":1455709,"title":"","content":"Re: faking being a Salubri, you can either say he hasn't learned Obeah/Valeren yet, and so doesn't have the third eye, or you could let him take it as a Merit/Flaw. They do share heritage, after all.<br /> <br /> That said, he could just as easily wear something over his forehead and pretend he has a third eye. Tattoo something there that looks like a closed eye, and that'll pass at a distance.<br /> <br /> If he ever takes any Infernal Investments, he could ask for a magical third eye to cement his disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:46:34-07:00","id":1464993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it#post1455312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Is it doable to have a Baali (or an infernalist) player character in a group when everybody is on board?</div> </div> </div> </div>Id argue you will have a much better experience when only the storyteller and the player who is a baali, know about it and the others dont. You can still make your questions about taboo topics, but i would not tell other players that one is a Baali. If they know beforehand their characters will likely &quot;immediately&quot; work it out at the first opportunity, they will somehow be aware that they are being corrupted and if the Baali is one day revealed as such it wont have any real impact on the players.<br /> It also limits the experience for the Baali player, cause he doesnt have to be nearly as careful hiding his true identity and likely wont even bother trying to corrupt the others.<br /> <br /> Only way i see it work well if everyone knows is, if the entire group plays as Baali<br /> <br /> 1) id recommend my ultimate baali summary thread for seeing options. &quot;The Baali&quot; as such doesnt exist and some like Molochim are way way better PC material than Nergali<br /> <br /> 2) You are the ST? You can limit them if they threaten your game. Demons may not want the Baali to have the investments after all.<br /> <br /> 3) Depends. For Playing a Baali clan book Baali is enough. Heck dark ages core rule book is enough. if you want all the lore, theres over a dozen books including werewolf ones mentioning baali and giving some background lore...which i hope have in said thread about baali summary to make it easier<br /> <br /> I also did a youtube series (sanguine archives) on the Baali from an IC perspective if you dont like reading ^^<br /> <br /> As general advice - depends as which clan you want to pose as. A true Molochim Baali will play 95% of his game as a legit character of the clan their character poses as. if you are a Baali infiltrating Clan Toreador, youll be playing a Toreador and be indistinguishable from a Toreador in RP. The devil is, literally, in the detail. Heck as Toreador Antitribu you might not even have to conceal much at all<br /> ...and for fairness, Nergali are playing chaotic stupid, which is sadly why many groups dont give Baali a chance. You can play Baali horriiiiiible. And the people playing them well are few and far between. <br /> <br /> Its Daimonion. Daimoinon was a typo that somehow caught on. But its a combination of a sweet snack and vegetable. Daim-onion. Welcome to a ruined discipline by dad joke<br /> <br /> Technicly you can make pacts with DTF demons i was on a crossover server where that worked very well for my Baali character. You dont have to read DTF for playing a Baali but, i would encourage it just you are aware of the different demon houses and factions cause your character surely would be aware of why its a bad idea to summon a reconciler or ravener.<br /> <br /> To Molochim and greater good....dont be fooled by that. Molochim want to prevent hell on earth yes...but because they want to rule the world and ruling the world isnt as nice when the world is fire and ashes. If you want to play a &quot;good&quot; Baali - Order of inner Light. Those are the only Baali that try to be good and redeem themselves in the eyes of god<br /> <br /> If you want to play &quot;a baali&quot; i found a good way to explain it is...play a Tremere with a sip of Setite and a hint of Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> For a tip how to lay a Baali well i recommend Ander Woods (Woodwwad) video on Nephandi. A Baali isnt going to tell you, he is whatever he needs to be to further his goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T06:26:39-07:00","id":1465003,"title":"","content":"I do recommend reading the rules for Thrall in DtF. Ignore the part about it not working on Vampires, it isn't necessarily true.<br /> <br /> What those rules will add to your game is the demon perspective and its tools to use the Thrall to its own ends. This helps in offering quick and versatile balances for eventual abuse on the Investments, letting you free to actually tempt the PC with power without XP cost or lessened cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T06:42:32-07:00","id":1465005,"title":"","content":"To infernal investments. Molochim kinda frown on making pacts. its not illegal, but its seen as a weakness, after all a true Lord has no master above himself, not even a demon. Pacts that Molochim enter, if they do, are usually of the sort that srews over the demon. and that tends to not go so well in the long run.<br /> <br /> That said Molochim are also in the Tal'mahe'ra<br /> <br /> I think i am att the point where i played more Baali characters than others. I now have a dark ages baali without disguise in tyre, 2 baali that pose as toreador, 1 baali tzimisce, 1 baali tremere and i am now creating a baali malkavian for a new chronicle.<br /> <br /> So far everyone i played with as Baali had a blast and was very intruiged by the lore behind the clan, and the performance ingame. And so far all my Baali characters are still alive and the one who was &quot;found out&quot; in character revealed himself to be Baali after he had the other player character in the pocket, after all he made her do all kinds of atrocities and thinking its for a greater good or actually good to do them. And after pointing out that she chose the road to damnation herself and walked it on her own feet not just willingly but enthusiasticly....i got myself an apostate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:27:31-07:00","id":1465059,"title":"","content":"Just remember that many, many times the worst action are not done out of malice but out of despair. <br /> Hardship can bring out the best , to a certain point; but when the suffering really becomes too much to bear, it moves even the best person to unthinkable actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:31:41-07:00","id":1465060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465005#post1465005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To infernal investments. Molochim kinda frown on making pacts. its not illegal, but its seen as a weakness, after all a true Lord has no master above himself, not even a demon. Pacts that Molochim enter, if they do, are usually of the sort that srews over the demon. and that tends to not go so well in the long run.<br /> <br /> That said Molochim are also in the Tal'mahe'ra</div> </div> </div> </div>I choose to believe the Baali being accepted is when the Nagaraja and Harbingers went, &quot;Nope. Bye.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T19:36:07-07:00","id":1465085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465060#post1465060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I choose to believe the Baali being accepted is when the Nagaraja and Harbingers went, &quot;Nope. Bye.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember the v20 Black Hand book retconned Enoch (and to a large extent the Black Hand) being obliterated by a spirit nuke. What's v5's take on that issue? Is Enoch and the Black Hand still around with Baali membership? Or did the Black Hand and Enoch get obliterated before that happened? <br /> <br /> Your take makes sense if v5 is using the v20 Black Hand, which the Baali joined, but it doesn't work if v5 retconned the v20 retcon about the Black Hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T00:52:02-07:00","id":1465103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1455363#post1455363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am probably unique in the fact that I don't see a reason why Infernalist Sabbat are any worse than regular Sabbat. Then again, my favorite game was Demon: The Fallen so I take the view that demons are not particularly worse than most supernaturals or humanity.<br /> <br /> Which is awful.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Worse? Arguable, but I can see why the Sabbat hate them, Infernalism is at it's core slavery, and the Sabbat are supposed to be about freedom","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:51:02-07:00","id":1465136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465085#post1465085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember the v20 Black Hand book retconned Enoch (and to a large extent the Black Hand) being obliterated by a spirit nuke. What's v5's take on that issue? Is Enoch and the Black Hand still around with Baali membership? Or did the Black Hand and Enoch get obliterated before that happened? <br /> <br /> Your take makes sense if v5 is using the v20 Black Hand, which the Baali joined, but it doesn't work if v5 retconned the v20 retcon about the Black Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20's Tal'mahe'ra book was a follow-through on that edition's promise of metaplot agnosticism. It presents an option in which the Underworld wasn't nuked and the Maelstrolm wasn't triggered. With the passage of that edition and the arrival of V5, metaplot is back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:10:11-07:00","id":1465140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465103#post1465103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse? Arguable, but I can see why the Sabbat hate them, Infernalism is at it's core slavery, and the Sabbat are supposed to be about freedom</div> </div> </div> </div>So, of course the Elders of the Sabbat hate competition.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T09:56:27-07:00","id":1465151,"title":"","content":"Demons don't add only servitude, they add for the Thrall another dangerous element: the Unknowable Purpose. This is an important piece of horror, where you have the constant uncertainty about the ultimate goal of your service.<br /> <br /> The Unknowable is different from the Unknown. You may not know the ultimate goal of your sire, prince, bishop or even Ante. But at least in principle we work with the idea that this goal is knowable, understandable and limited in some scope, even if it may be irrational, abhorrent and ambitious.<br /> <br /> But demons seem to operate in another level even for Methuselah. They act and scheme in the highest scope possible, their goals can be only be grasped on legends. You know not what you're serving or to what end it uses you.<br /> <br /> And that's scary and give the impression of ultimate evil, even if it is actually just asking for lemonade because it is tasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:37:12-07:00","id":1465162,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that demons, in exchange for sacrifices and your soul, can also turn a otherwise useless shovelhead into a vampire as powerful as an Ancilla or Elder. Another reason to be afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T13:52:03-07:00","id":1465179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it#post1455312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Is it doable to have a Baali (or an infernalist) player character in a group when everybody is on board?<br /> We have at our disposal clanbook - baali (black dog), all the V20 books and from storyteller vault the 2 books related to baali.<br /> We also have path of screams, book of madness and devil's due from old lines to look into. (have been playing for well over 2 decades) <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are there any tips and tricks to make this work? (except of course the part about don't go into details which should remain unnamed and we have easy stops if it should not work out,...) I'm asking cause this is the first time we are going to play the &quot;bad guys&quot;, if there is something like good guys in the world of darkness....</li> <li>Is there any way to make demonic investments works because as they have no XP component, they scale pretty harshly?</li> <li>Are there any other books we might need?</li> </ol><br /> Thank you very much for any and all advice even if it's, don't do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't read the rest of the thread. Here are my two cents.<br /> <br /> From personal experience, there's not a whole lot that an infernalist can do that &quot;normal&quot; PCs won't in a regular game. PC vampires will regularly kill people for petty reasons, torture suspects to get information, steal, engage in corruption, and do a whole lot of heinous shit. So draw the line not with the characters, but with the players. Human sacrifices most certainly won't cause trouble with your group. Raping babies would. Negotiate where the &quot;we don't do this ever&quot; line is, and don't cross it. Just talk to people about it. Talking is good.<br /> <br /> Forget about the existing rules for investments. Talk to your infernalist player about what he wants to do as an infernalist, and what he wants to get out of being an infernalist. E.g., I like infernalists a whole lot because I like demons as a concept. My end goal in playing an infernalist is to interact with demons and do demon-y things. Getting an NPC to sell their soul - that's a reward in of itself!<br /> Once you've learned what the player wants to get, you can tailor the rewards the group gets without heaping extras on top. Maybe everyone gets a personalized reward from the story, and the infernalist's are the investments from their patron. Or the infernalist trades part of their soul (in form of xp). Or something else. IMHO, infernal boons as part of the story reward are easier to balance than infernal boons as a separate abuseable mechanic.<br /> Books can be used for inspiration for the boons I guess.<br /> <br /> Discuss with the non-infernalist players what is keeping the group together. The allure of being a secret infernalist is strong, but IMHO, not worth it. It just means you spend less time actually playing an infernalist because all the time in the party is spent pretending that you aren't one. And at least the players definitely should know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T20:16:37-07:00","id":1465238,"title":"","content":"In THE STORYTELLER'S GUIDE TO THE SABBAT, a demon that was previously only offered cats as sacrifices was found by the Sabbat who gave it much bigger sacrifices. The demon was confused how to proceed with worshipers who were already irredeemably evil.<br /> <br /> I always thought that was a cute story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-25-2021, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T20:53:00-07:00","id":1465239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465140#post1465140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, of course the Elders of the Sabbat hate competition.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Partially yes, but at the base most Sabbat at least partially believe in the war against the Antes, and infernalists swap being tools of the Antes for being the tools of something just as bad and older ..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:14:02-07:00","id":1465290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465238#post1465238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In THE STORYTELLER'S GUIDE TO THE SABBAT, a demon that was previously only offered cats as sacrifices was found by the Sabbat who gave it much bigger sacrifices. The demon was confused how to proceed with worshipers who were already irredeemably evil.<br /> <br /> I always thought that was a cute story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so good that Revised did away with cartoonisly and irredeemably evil Sabbat and they are absent in V5... oh, wait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:56:16-07:00","id":1465333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465290#post1465290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's so good that Revised did away with cartoonisly and irredeemably evil Sabbat and they are absent in V5... oh, wait</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, what?<br /> <br /> Revised was specifically made because Justin Achilli thought 2nd Edition had made the Sabbat lose its edge. The Sabbat in The Guide to the Sabbat actually <i>call themselves</i> evil. The book made the Camarilla worse and highlighted what horrible hellholes any city with the Sabbat in them were. 1999's Clan Novels were also about depicting the Sabbat as a ravening horde of locusts.<br /> <br /> The mindless Beast ridden Sabbat taking over was always a problem the Sabbat had to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T21:36:33-07:00","id":1465354,"title":"","content":"I like horrendous villains<br /> <br /> But the larger they are, the more important they avoid that sense of &quot;too evil/stupid to function&quot;<br /> <br /> Which both the Camarilla and Sabbat fall into with V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T02:00:26-07:00","id":1465371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465333#post1465333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, what?<br /> <br /> Revised was specifically made because Justin Achilli thought 2nd Edition had made the Sabbat lose its edge. The Sabbat in The Guide to the Sabbat actually <i>call themselves</i> evil. The book made the Camarilla worse and highlighted what horrible hellholes any city with the Sabbat in them were. 1999's Clan Novels were also about depicting the Sabbat as a ravening horde of locusts.<br /> <br /> The mindless Beast ridden Sabbat taking over was always a problem the Sabbat had to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help that Achilli is stuck mentally in 1ed when it comes to Sabbat. I was happy when we left the mwahaha evil Sabbat behind and got more complex and nuanced vampire organization. &quot;Evil because&quot; villains can work but are usually boring, especially in Vampire which is about the shades of grey.<br /> <br /> YMMV but I don't think that Sabbat think of themselves as evil (unless they are on the Path of Evil Revelations but what can you do). That's the point of the Paths of Enlightment. <br /> <br /> I do not think that was an issue. Mindless Sabbat were locked in the cellar and released on unsuspecting Cam during crusades. <br /> <br /> That's my take, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T02:16:17-07:00","id":1465372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465371#post1465371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't help that Achilli is stuck mentally in 1ed when it comes to Sabbat. I was happy when we left the mwahaha evil Sabbat behind and got more complex and nuanced vampire organization. &quot;Evil because&quot; villains can work but are usually boring, especially in Vampire which is about the shades of grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that if you're the developer that you can say you're stuck in a mentality. Also, if the Sabbat really are mindless horrifying killing machines in 1st, Revised, and 5th.<br /> <br /> Then is it an alternate interpretation or you just really like 2nd Edition?<br /> <br /> Because at some point, you might just acknowledge that's who they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> YMMV but I don't think that Sabbat think of themselves as evil (unless they are on the Path of Evil Revelations but what can you do). That's the point of the Paths of Enlightment.<br /> <br /> I do not think that was an issue. Mindless Sabbat were locked in the cellar and released on unsuspecting Cam during crusades.<br /> <br /> That's my take, anyway. </div> </div> </div>That is very much 2nd Edition's take. Revised, for whatever reason, had the Sabbat shout, &quot;We're evil! You're Damned! Revel in it!&quot; Which is a bit...on the nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T03:05:47-07:00","id":1465373,"title":"","content":"I like the diversity. Just like with the Baali - yeah there are stupid evil Baali...they dont live long. Just like there are truly dysfunctional Malkavians. They dont get much time to live either. And there are beast controlled Sabbath...same story.<br /> <br /> I can see the sabbath having &quot;sub factions&quot; just like the Baali. and i can see them disagreeing on quite some issues. Heck they had that with the black hand and stuff anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T04:45:58-07:00","id":1465379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465372#post1465372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if the Sabbat really are mindless horrifying killing machines in 1st, Revised, and 5th.<br /> <br /> Then is it an alternate interpretation or you just really like 2nd Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br /> <br /> I just like 2nd ed Sabbat and that seems to be a common opinion among the people that enjoy playing as Sabbat (not saying it is the only opinion, I know you do).<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition made the Sabbat nuanced and that seems to be the major criticism regardless of edition: the problem is taking out nuance, not if it is &quot;the true&quot; Sabbat. If the nuanced Sabbat is only 2nd ed, why not, then I only like it in 2nd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T04:56:43-07:00","id":1465381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465372#post1465372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that if you're the developer that you can say you're stuck in a mentality. Also, if the Sabbat really are mindless horrifying killing machines in 1st, Revised, and 5th.<br /> <br /> Then is it an alternate interpretation or you just really like 2nd Edition?<br /> <br /> Because at some point, you might just acknowledge that's who they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is very much 2nd Edition's take. Revised, for whatever reason, had the Sabbat shout, &quot;We're evil! You're Damned! Revel in it!&quot; Which is a bit...on the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure that you can say Achilli is stuck in his &quot;Sabbat is Eeevul&quot; mentality. I just did as much.<br /> <br /> I have mainly played in 2ed-early Revised era but I have gripes with both. I really do not remember GTTS presenting Sabbat as one dimensional evil, granted it has been probably 10+ years since I have read the book last time. If it did then that's just another strike against Achilli.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it doesn't matter if Achilli's vision fot Sabbat is ib agreement with Sabbat's presentation for most of VtM's life. What matters is that is a shallow and boring vision not suitable for my Vampire games. I am sure that sime people will agree and others may not. But that's how I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T06:41:31-07:00","id":1465388,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of another fandom I'm a part of with the STAR WARS universe and roleplaying game. One of the most popular villains of the Expanded Universe was Grand Admiral Thrawn who was a nuanced and fascinating character who presented the &quot;reasonable&quot; side of the Empire. So much so that the Empire started getting a lot of its own comics, books, and stories. There were also people who unironically argued the Empire just had some bad eggs.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it started hitting its nadir with Dark Horse comics STAR WARS: LEGACY where they had originally intended to write out the Jedi Knights and have Imperial Knights with the ending of the final timeline story in the EU being the rise of a new benevolent Solo-descended Empress.<br /> And fans HATED THIS.<br /> <br /> The obvious reaosn being that while the Imperial fans were a significant minority, the fact was that the &quot;nuanced&quot; Empire took away from the fact they were inspired by, well, all of the worst elements of empires in RL. They were ranting comic book villains and that by portraying them as misunderstood law and order types, you weren't adding nuance. No, you were simply <i>rewriting</i> them.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting balance to strike because I feel like that if you remove the awful parts of an organization in the World of Darkness, you aren't adding nuance. You're not even being a fan of the group because that's not the group. The Sabbat were created for the purposes of allowing vampires who were able to do the things that, by the rules, other vampires would hit wassail for.<br /> <br /> To use the immortal scene from <i>Near Dark</i>, the Sabbat exist so that a group of vampires can go into a bar and proceed to kill every single human in there for fun. There is no greater reason or purpose. It is to revel in the screams, terror, and helplessness of mortals that die for no reason other than a monster's hunger. That is boring as fuck if that is ALL the Sabbat is. The Sabbat is many things: post human philosophers, Noddist scholars, mystics of dark forces, and a militant theocratic army for Caine.<br /> <br /> But being an absolute violent evil asshole that would herd humans into camps to bleed like cows are milked is PART of what the Sabbat is. It's one of the things that I feel like was lost with some of the Post-Revised Technocracy. The Technocracy should have nuance, should be able to explain their goals in a coherent rationale manner. The mark of a good villain is that they can summarize how they got from Point A to Point B even if it's, &quot;As a Bond villain I'm rich as fuck and get all the ladies and henchmen.&quot; But the Union should still be the guys who murder supernaturals indiscriminately, torture, brainwash, clone, and oppress.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of the Sabbat in V5 totally. I feel they have ditched a lot of what makes the sect unique but the Sabbat should never NOT be the most overtly evil and monstrous of Kindred. That is their thing and you shouldn't take that away from them.<br /> <br /> Part of what I love playing a Sabbat is being the &quot;Only Sane Man&quot; and my Sabbat games are often like my THE OLD REPUBLIC games where you are the only Sith Lord who isn't an self-defeating schoolyard bully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-26-2021, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T06:53:22-07:00","id":1465391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465371#post1465371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't help that Achilli is stuck mentally in 1ed when it comes to Sabbat. I was happy when we left the mwahaha evil Sabbat behind and got more complex and nuanced vampire organization. &quot;Evil because&quot; villains can work but are usually boring, especially in Vampire which is about the shades of grey.<br /> <br /> YMMV but I don't think that Sabbat think of themselves as evil (unless they are on the Path of Evil Revelations but what can you do). That's the point of the Paths of Enlightment.<br /> <br /> I do not think that was an issue. Mindless Sabbat were locked in the cellar and released on unsuspecting Cam during crusades.<br /> <br /> That's my take, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How can Achilli be stuck mentally in 1ed when it comes to Sabbat, when he has written 3ed Revised Sabbat ? Isn't he the one who gave us the nuanced Sabbat with many different factions, who was engaged in worldwide war against the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> Paths of Enlightenment were described as &quot;EEEEVIL&quot; in 2 Edition, when you had &quot;Callousness&quot; as a Virtue, but also in Revised, when you had to crush your Humanity at least to 3, to join one, even the moderately benign Honorable Accord or Harmony. And to reach Humanity 3, you have to be a serial murderer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T07:00:48-07:00","id":1465393,"title":"","content":"Some rules I've used for Roleplaying my Infernalist characters:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Infernalists are rational</b><br /> <br /> There are a bunch of bug fuck nuts evil demon-worshipers out there. Generally, you are not one of these people.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Infernalists have a decent argument to worship demons</b><br /> <br /> You are a vampire, you are Damned. Therefore, there is no risk to damning yourself more. There is also much profit to gain.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Infernalists get good bang for their buck</b><br /> <br /> A good infernalist knows that research is key with demons. Some are untrustworthy bastards while others will give you exactly what you want as long as you pay the price. The trick is being smart enough to know which is which.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Psychopaths kill for no reason, Infernalists kill for power</b><br /> <br /> Yes, I quoted Grosse Pointe Blank. An Infernalist might revel in torture and evil like a Sabbat but most will be the quiet type who is measuring how many human souls he can trade for that extra Infernal investment.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Infernalist religion makes internal sense</b><br /> <br /> God is evil<br /> Demons are evil<br /> One of them pays you if you work for them. God ignores you.<br /> <br /> Which do you think is worth worshiping?<br /> <br /> It certainly works better than Caine who ignores you and is evil.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Infernalists can have friends</b><br /> <br /> After all, we're all damned here.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>This is just a game so have fun with playing your evil sorcerer</b><br /> <br /> Nuff said.<br /> <br /> 8.<b> Infernalists are not slaves, well anymore than any other religion</b><br /> <br /> As Dracula says in Symphony of the Night. Belial is not going to dictate how you do your nights. The Sabbat does. Its thus a nonsensical distinction. You worship the Queen of Thorned Whips because you like what she's selling.<br /> <br /> 9. <b>You may have sold your soul but you're more likely to have PLEDGED IT.</b><br /> <br /> An important distinction. Besides, you're going to Hell when you die anyway and as a vampire you can maybe buy it back, become a demon yourself, or so on.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Fight fire with fire</b><br /> <br /> The Sabbat cannot beat the Antediluvians. Maybe Kupala can.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-26-2021, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T10:10:32-07:00","id":1465416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465388#post1465388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by portraying them as misunderstood law and order types, you weren't adding nuance. No, you were simply <i>rewriting</i> them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where you seem to miss the point.<br /> <br /> No one here wants a Sabbat that can't be awfully evil. A nuanced Sabbat can still have literal human farms and nights of wanton murder for giggles.<br /> <br /> But there's a big difference between this being possible, this being the whole point, and this being an obligation. Between a sect where any member can do that once in a while and some may do that 'most every night, and a sect where everyone's required to attend the weekly blood pool party.<br /> <br /> Adding to that, many fans just don't care about the proposed tropes to the point of ignoring their most obvious logical conclusions. The Whole Evil Sabbat and Technocracy are dumb. I feel as an ST my game being intellectually drained if I have to reconcile it with the very notion of such idiotic concepts existing in the same world. So a Sabbat nuanced enough for me to adjust the gore level to my needs without having to &quot;houserule&quot; is a win, and may even be good enough for me to enjoy playing Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> 'Cause, you know, I find the constant gorefest boring. But V5 made it a point to say that I can't have my style of Sabbat and that I have to play in a world where the gorefest is all over the place and somehow weren't wiped out yet. First thing to do in any game I ever have to ST with this retarded Sabbat version is to wipe it out since it doesn't make sense to me and isn't interesting either.<br /> <br /> It is not about having a nuanced Sabbat because we want a different take on the Sabbat to take over. It definitely is about wanting a nuanced Sabbat because for most of us the non-nuanced Sabbat is boring and we'll pass. But that also forces us to throw away a lot of potential in the idea beyond the retarded evil. Above all, it is about wanting a nuanced Sabbat that lets the ST adjust the Sabbat to their chronicle instead of playing with only one set the authors deem the only right way to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T15:21:19-07:00","id":1465443,"title":"","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I thought it would be a good idea to have an official place to discuss product from the Storyteller's Vault, recommend your favorite pieces, and critique the ones that you feel are worth modifying for your campaigns. I feel like with the addition of 5th Edition material to the product that it has a bigger relevence to the fandom (and it had a pretty big one before). Which is to say that there is value to the setting element that some Sabbat are soccer hooligans. One of the elements that is intristic to the setting is the loss of Humanity to become degenerate animalistic killers. To see the higher functions and genius of the vampire lost to become ravenous brutal monsters enslaved to their appetites.<br /> <br /> I feel one of the things necessary in the Sabbat isn't that they're 'evil' but the fact the Sabbat must struggle to lose their fight against the Beast and the extreme diablerie-happy mindless violence as well as fanaticism that infects their sect. Not everyone in the Sabbat can or should be able to master the Beasts via Paths of Enlightenment but will dwell near the bottom of it. I feel like one of the struggles the Sabbat and Sabbat characters shiould have to deal with is the members of their sect who are pointlessly sadistic and evil monsters. The ones dragging down the sect with their massacres and revelries of destruction. The hunger fo diablerie and Beast that threatens all.<br /> <br /> Because the question becomes, &quot;Is the Sabbat worth saving?&quot; or &quot;Is this just the true face of vampires?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;The nuance is great but it should be nuance with room for ravenous half-feral monsters like 30 Days of Night.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also agree the new Sabbat need more enlightened philosopher kings too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-26-2021, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T00:02:24-07:00","id":1465483,"title":"","content":"To me the key to the Sabbat is to stop thinking of homo sapiens are inherently more sacred than any other species. Homo sapiens are not sacred. Homo sapiens are just the ape that happened to win. Once you take that as a given, then vampires' treatment of homo sapiens ceases to be relevant. What matters is how do you construct a society of vampires designed around vampire needs? Whether actions are evil or not then become about whether those actions are constructive to a vampire society, not about what effect it has on homo sapiens, as homo sapiens are no more relevant than trees in this context.<br /> <br /> The treatment of homo sapiens is therefore only relevant in an extremely indirect way. If you found someone torturing a doughnut and twirling their moustache, you wouldn't call them &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;monsterous&quot;, but you would consider them irrational and foolish and even goofy. It's a doughnut. Why are you torturing a doughnut? I mean, it's a doughnut for Caine's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 10-27-2021, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T00:34:55-07:00","id":1465485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465483#post1465483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the key to the Sabbat is to stop thinking of homo sapiens are inherently more sacred than any other species. Homo sapiens are not sacred. Homo sapiens are just the ape that happened to win. Once you take that as a given, then vampires' treatment of homo sapiens ceases to be relevant. What matters is how do you construct a society of vampires designed around vampire needs? Whether actions are evil or not then become about whether those actions are constructive to a vampire society, not about what effect it has on homo sapiens, as homo sapiens are no more relevant than trees in this context.<br /> <br /> The treatment of homo sapiens is therefore only relevant in an extremely indirect way. If you found someone torturing a doughnut and twirling their moustache, you wouldn't call them &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;monsterous&amp;quot;, but you would consider them irrational and foolish and even goofy. It's a doughnut. Why are you torturing a doughnut? I mean, it's a doughnut for Caine's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except people are not doughnuts in this metaphor, rather chickens or cows and most people think torturing cows is evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T01:22:10-07:00","id":1465487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465483#post1465483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the key to the Sabbat is to stop thinking of homo sapiens are inherently more sacred than any other species. Homo sapiens are not sacred. Homo sapiens are just the ape that happened to win. Once you take that as a given, then vampires' treatment of homo sapiens ceases to be relevant. What matters is how do you construct a society of vampires designed around vampire needs? Whether actions are evil or not then become about whether those actions are constructive to a vampire society, not about what effect it has on homo sapiens, as homo sapiens are no more relevant than trees in this context.<br /> <br /> The treatment of homo sapiens is therefore only relevant in an extremely indirect way. If you found someone torturing a doughnut and twirling their moustache, you wouldn't call them &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;monsterous&quot;, but you would consider them irrational and foolish and even goofy. It's a doughnut. Why are you torturing a doughnut? I mean, it's a doughnut for Caine's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry but why this approach shouldn't be &quot;evil&quot;? It's basically Real-Life Suprematism with Vampires and Humans instead that Races. It is an interesting topic to explore, but nonetheless it's very much evil.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nuance&quot; in the Sabbat should be about tactics, philosophies, and ways of expressing this suprematist point of view: not about condoning Sabbat ideology as something &quot;acceptable&quot;. It is interesting to contrast Heidegger against a brownshirt thug, but they both adhere to a philosophy of evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T03:30:15-07:00","id":1465490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465483#post1465483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the key to the Sabbat is to stop thinking of homo sapiens are inherently more sacred than any other species. Homo sapiens are not sacred. Homo sapiens are just the ape that happened to win. Once you take that as a given, then vampires' treatment of homo sapiens ceases to be relevant. What matters is how do you construct a society of vampires designed around vampire needs? Whether actions are evil or not then become about whether those actions are constructive to a vampire society, not about what effect it has on homo sapiens, as homo sapiens are no more relevant than trees in this context.<br /> <br /> The treatment of homo sapiens is therefore only relevant in an extremely indirect way. If you found someone torturing a doughnut and twirling their moustache, you wouldn't call them &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;monsterous&quot;, but you would consider them irrational and foolish and even goofy. It's a doughnut. Why are you torturing a doughnut? I mean, it's a doughnut for Caine's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that is an interesting angle to pursue but the Sabbat are a theological sect. It is not that humans are less sacred than animals. It is that vampires are very much so and view them their prey. And I did like Justin Achili saying, &quot;Sabbat do not treat humans like cattle. The Camarilla treats humans like cattle. Sabbat treat humans like a shark treats fish.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even that may not explain away the fact the Sabbat revel in the fear and terror of waging war upon the race they are apart from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465487#post1465487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but why this approach shouldn't be &quot;evil&quot;? It's basically Real-Life Suprematism with Vampires and Humans instead that Races. It is an interesting topic to explore, but nonetheless it's very much evil.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nuance&quot; in the Sabbat should be about tactics, philosophies, and ways of expressing this suprematist point of view: not about condoning Sabbat ideology as something &quot;acceptable&quot;. It is interesting to contrast Heidegger against a brownshirt thug, but they both adhere to a philosophy of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mindset of the Sabbat is an important thing to understand.<br /> <br /> And let's face it, it's not humans are &quot;real&quot; people.<br /> <br /> They die so quickly.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:32:59-07:00","id":1465496,"title":"","content":"<b>Another Set of Tips for Running Infernalist Chronicles</b><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Evil versus Evil</b><br /> <br /> There's a bunch of competing Demon Lords, Infernalists, and monsters out there to fight.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Use Demon: The Fallen for creating Patrons</b><br /> <br /> There's a lot more nuance and interesting twists you can do by having the player character's demonic patron not necessarily fit into the stereotype of Bwa-ha-ha-ha evil.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Infernalists are not Nephandi</b><br /> <br /> You can have them want to destroy the world but plenty of them are much like Spike. <i>&quot;We like to talk big, vampires do. &quot;I'm going to destroy the world.&quot; It's just tough-guy talk. Struttin' around with your friends over a pint of blood. The truth is, I *like* this world. You've got... dog racing, Manchester United... and you've got people. Billions of people walking around like Happy Meals with legs. It's all right here... But then, someone comes along with a vision. With a real... passion for destruction... Angel could pull it off. Goodbye Piccadilly, farewell Leicester bloody Square. You know what I'm saying? &quot;</i><br /> <br /> 4. <b>Personal Revenge</b><br /> <br /> As an infernalist in the Sabbat or Baali, there's undoubtedly some assholes you want to destroy with your power. Maybe you ARE worse than the Prince who had your mortal family killed because<br /> you talked to them about being a vampire or the Sabbat bishop who Embraced you against your will but that doesn't mean it won't be satisfying destroying them.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Demons vs. Cthulhu</b><br /> <br /> Worshiping the Devil may seem to be the worst thing you can do but at least they are...human. There are things that are incomprehensible creatures of madness and chaos out there and preventing them from unmaking creation is a good idea.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Are the demons using you or are you using the Demons?</b><br /> <br /> This is a theme worth exploring.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Power Gaming is permitted</b><br /> <br /> A Infernalist actually will do a lot to sink their EXP into Dark Thaumaturgy/Blood Sorcery. This isn't a bad thing as they are people who measure how much they've succeeded in their level of personal power.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Infernalists still struggle with the Beast</b><br /> <br /> Being a monster doesn't mean you don't have to worry about becoming a mindless monster. You may also have a few Darth Vader-esque regrets. But you have COME TOO FAR TO BACK DOWN NOW!<br /> <br /> 9. <b>Good guys being Knight Templar fanatics</b><br /> <br /> Make use of the Templars, Society of Leopold, Werewolves, Imbued, and so on.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Downtime is always fun</b><br /> <br /> Some demon worshipers just hanging around having a beer is hilarious by itself sometimes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:40:10-07:00","id":1465497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465483#post1465483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the key to the Sabbat is to stop thinking of homo sapiens are inherently more sacred than any other species. Homo sapiens are not sacred..</div> </div> </div> </div>In Context with the WoD, you're actually <i>wrong</i>. <br /> Animals can't be made into vampires. Homo Sapiens are the only thing in the WoD that can be embraced into the Cainite race (or awaken as a mage) Well, like, maybe our Vampires are older than we though and our hypothetical Caine is a <i>Neanderthal</i> vampire or some other extinct near human, but those aren't around around anymore and we can't find Caine, so we can't really say. Of the Apes we do have access to, they can't be made into vampires. There's just something <i>missing</i> there. Those crazy mages trying to make <i>Homo Superior</i>? The products can't awaken, and presumably can't be made into vampires. <br /> <br /> Humans are quantifiably special in the WoD. lending credence to God's image and all that. I can't say if it works like that in real life, but canonically, we are the chosen species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:58:38-07:00","id":1465498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465497#post1465497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Context with the WoD, you're actually <i>wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you are correct ofc, i think what Khan meant is that sabbath see themselves as so far superior to humans, that humans are actually just cattle to them. It makes sense for many vampires to think so even if the sheer existance of mages proves them wrong.<br /> <br /> And sure, sabbath see humans as nourishment. That said....humans eat animals too and sure only some vegans raise a stink if you eat a hamburger. HOWEVER if you were caught brutally eviscerating and disfiguring cows int he most gruesome ways before eating them still alive....yeah...you stick out and in most countries on the planet this would be a felony and id say there is extremely few people who wouldnt see the problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T05:05:34-07:00","id":1465500,"title":"","content":"What is your Baali's goal? Basically.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do they make compact with the Beast?&quot;<br /> <br /> Riches, revenge, loneliness, or genuine religious ecstasy?<br /> <br /> Define that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T05:07:11-07:00","id":1465501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465496#post1465496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Another Set of Tips for Running Infernalist Chronicles</b><br /> 6. <b>Are the demons using you or are you using the Demons?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Actuall that was answered for the Baali somewhat.<br /> <br /> Demons use Nergali<br /> Molochim use Demons against demons<br /> The Wyrm uses the swarm<br /> The Azaneali use the Abyss<br /> <br /> Destroyers use demons and are used by them<br /> Celestials use demons<br /> Children of Enigma dont give a damn about demons<br /> Order of the inner Light fights against demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T05:13:22-07:00","id":1465502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465500#post1465500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your Baali's goal? Basically.<br /> Define that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal motivations aside that are important ofc<br /> <br /> Destroyers - want revenge on the world that was cruel to them and just wanna burn it to cinders. Go well alongside Raveners<br /> Celestials - want to ascend vampirism and become true immortals. Becoming a demon is just a stepping stone to getting a type of ascension similiar to mages, or even get their divine spark back<br /> Children of Enigma - want knowledge. They want to understand reality as much as they can and research...no morals holding them back<br /> Order of the inner light wants redemption and get back on gods good side<br /> <br /> Nergali want to become true demons themselves and rule the world....similiar to tzimisce. just way worse<br /> Molochim want to rule the world from behind the scenes like Tremere and shape it...thus they first must make sure it aint destroyed by demons.<br /> The swarm wants to change the world to the likings of the wyrm and defile it. Destroying the world wouldnt be justice, it has to suffer as they did<br /> Azaneali, similiar to abyss mystics, prefer to gain power through knowledge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:45:05-07:00","id":1465522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465501#post1465501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Molochim use Demons against demons<br /> Destroyers use demons and are used by them<br /> Celestials use demons</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are not necessarily true. The Baali thinking they understand demons enough to be sure of what they're doing doesn't necessarily mean they got it right.<br /> <br /> If you step in and declare OoC they are, you just smash a potential plot for no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:46:17-07:00","id":1465531,"title":"","content":"well sure the Baali get screwed over too, occasionally. I meant they try to do it these ways ^^ and, Baali have a better chance of getting it right than any other infernalist, at least thats my oppinion on it given they do this since milennia and study it so deeply not only did at least one of them become a full demon but one demon actually became a baali too (mary the black)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T11:51:39-07:00","id":1465543,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is that you take out a lot of the sting of infernalism and its strength as a theme if you just assume they got it right, and eliminates story options. You also can't say it for sure based only on knowledge from the PoV of the Baali themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:08:29-07:00","id":1465545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465543#post1465543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is that you take out a lot of the sting of infernalism and its strength as a theme if you just assume they got it right, and eliminates story options. You also can't say it for sure based only on knowledge from the PoV of the Baali themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that is very unclear in my games is that the Baali THINK they are keeping the Children asleep by their regular sacrifices to them. It's equally possible they're empowering them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T02:11:50-07:00","id":1465614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465545#post1465545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that is very unclear in my games is that the Baali THINK they are keeping the Children asleep by their regular sacrifices to them. It's equally possible they're empowering them.</div> </div> </div> </div>id say they even know that as a fact, but do it anyway cause they hope it keeps them asleep, and as long as they sleep making them more powerfull isnt a problem. And if they awake thery end the world even with less power. so...<br /> <br /> Thing is we know sacrifices strenghten demons, im pretty sure Baali are aware of how pacts and thralls work at least to an extend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T02:23:27-07:00","id":1465615,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I roughly categorize different infernalists as such:<br /> <br /> The Confused: Think they're infernalists, aren't actually calling on the infernal, somehow got magic working. Would probably lose their Trial.<br /> <br /> True thralls: Completely sold themselves. The master has overridden what gives them pleasure and pain. Working on behalf of the master gives them the greatest of joy, and they'll happily discomfort themselves if it's in the demon's interest. If the demon isn't around and it's interests aren't involved, usually absolutely indistinguishable from how they were before they sold themselves. (demons may give them bizzare kinks or derangements for fun, they may even allow the victim to keep their emotions unmolested and experience the horror of lacking free will, but usually they're sleeper agents waiting to be used or prostituted to a client)<br /> <br /> Standard Bargain: Both sides have made agreements. No clear winner. One side may be trying to get advantage over the other. Usually the mortal tries to get out of their obligations or the demon tries to get the mortal into debt.. but the reverse also happens. or they might recognize a one-time deal and leave eachother alone.<br /> <br /> Happy Capitalist: They've made a deal. The Summoner tries to push the demon into more service or more deals. The two sides have a lot to offer one another without crossing bottom lines.<br /> <br /> Master of Demons: The Mortal has enslaved the demon through either true name exploitation or by exploiting an arrangement. They can draw upon the demon's power at will without selling themselves. The demon can try to retaliate by using what freedoms it hasn't been denied to screw over the master. Other demons and would be supplicants will try to &quot;rescue&quot; such an enslaved demon, the former in part out of principle, but in general a gratefully rescued demon is expected to offer good rewards. Generally the rarest type, as it takes lots of research and cunning to get here and then to clamp down on the demon, things can go very wrong, and masters are generally the most threatening category so their persecution is actually worse than those who submit to demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-28-2021, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T05:33:27-07:00","id":1465626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465614#post1465614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is we know sacrifices strenghten demons, im pretty sure Baali are aware of how pacts and thralls work at least to an extend</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting bit: in DtF sacrifices don't do shit to Demons. They're useful as window-dressing, to hide their real agenda and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:18:47-07:00","id":1465631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465626#post1465626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting bit: in DtF sacrifices don't do shit to Demons. They're useful as window-dressing, to hide their real agenda and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was not the case and a sacarifce gives a boost of faith from the person for a one time gift.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T07:05:27-07:00","id":1465644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465631#post1465631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was not the case and a sacarifce gives a boost of faith from the person for a one time gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is in some supplement and I didn't saw it when I read, no.<br /> <br /> Sacrifices do nothing at all.<br /> <br /> But a person's mindset during the pact or when reaping Faith is paramount, so window-dressing <b>is</b> important.<br /> <br /> If you're not in the right state of awe, it simply doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T10:50:00-07:00","id":1465670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465631#post1465631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was not the case and a sacarifce gives a boost of faith from the person for a one time gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is reaving a thrall (I think the term is reaving anyway, been a while since I have read it). Basically you 'eat' a Thrall for Faith 'right now' but it destroys the as a future source. Sacrifice isn't really that useful for Faith directly, but it is great for unifying a cult and weeding out the unsure, they are accessories to murder and kidnap now, and if they run they are next under the knife..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:13:24-07:00","id":1465686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465500#post1465500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your Baali's goal? Basically.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Why do they make compact with the Beast?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Riches, revenge, loneliness, or genuine religious ecstasy?<br /> <br /> Define that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s only one in my campaign and his goal is to prove that everyone else is just as big a monster as he is and that he is unique only in his raw power (he\u2019s the lowest gen vampire in the city), not that his base motives are any worse than anyone else\u2019s\u2026 that even those with access to a fraction of his power would use it for wickedness. Every sin he allows others to indulge in using his resources is just more proof that all men are monsters and he\u2019s, well, he\u2019s not so bad after all.<br /> <br /> He utterly loathes anyone of True Faith or anyone with power who uses it selflessly because it pokes a giant hole in his personal narrative. He throws everything he can at them to try and break them and prove they\u2019re just as bad and are only deluding themselves.<br /> <br /> The Baali\u2019s particular bloodline weakness galls him and he\u2019s convinced that the effect is ultimately some form of magical trickery (he is a master of the path of spirit manipulation so he\u2019s inclined to think it\u2019s some sort of hostile spirits with a vendetta against vampires that is using its power on them rather than genuine goodness being a real thing that can repel him).<br /> <br /> Honestly, if he ever had to consciously acknowledge that someone really was genuinely good to their core he\u2019d probably crash right down into Wassail and flame out soon after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:35:19-07:00","id":1465697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455312-baali-or-infernalists-as-player-characters-doable-or-not-and-how-do-you-do-it?p=1465686#post1465686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Baali\u2019s particular bloodline weakness galls him and he\u2019s convinced that the effect is ultimately some form of magical trickery (he is a master of the path of spirit manipulation so he\u2019s inclined to think it\u2019s some sort of hostile spirits with a vendetta against vampires that is using its power on them rather than genuine goodness being a real thing that can repel him).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's entirely possible he's not wrong about that. I've seen White Wolf material go both ways about True Faith being a manifestation of <i>just</i> the believer's own devotion and spiritual purity, or being an answer from divine forces reacting to same. From a certain point of view Yahweh and His angels fit into the Celestine &gt; Incarna &gt; Jaggling &gt; Gaffling system same as any other group of related spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}